WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.165
Prepare offline maps while you still have an internet connection.

00:00:04.165 --> 00:00:08.266
In RID2Caltopo, open the operational map and pan and zoom to the

00:00:08.266 --> 00:00:09.163
area you need.

00:00:09.163 --> 00:00:13.200
You can also choose an available map boundary in the next step.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.798
Open the map settings gear and choose Download Map.

00:00:16.798 --> 00:00:21.714
Under Area, choose Current Visible Map, or select an available map boundary.

00:00:21.714 --> 00:00:25.400
The download uses the selected area’s bounding rectangle.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:30.988
Choose USGS Scanned Topo or USFS Topo, and set the zoom levels you need.

00:00:30.988 --> 00:00:36.644
You can also include Contours, DEM elevation data, and one-meter AOL obstacle

00:00:36.644 --> 00:00:37.966
tiles when needed.

00:00:37.966 --> 00:00:42.300
Larger areas and higher detail require more time and space.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.972
Review the estimated download and available storage.

00:00:45.972 --> 00:00:49.799
Reduce the area or detail, or adjust the map cache limit in

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:51.420
Manage Storage if needed.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.403
Tap Start and wait for the download to finish.

00:00:54.403 --> 00:00:58.100
If anything fails, use Retry before leaving connectivity.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.094
To share eligible cached data, frame the area on the map.

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:06.956
Open the map settings gear, choose Map Management, then Export Map Package.

00:01:06.956 --> 00:01:10.391
Select the data you need and tap Prepare Map Package.

00:01:10.391 --> 00:01:15.900
Export uses cached data in the current visible region; it does not download anything.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:22.522
By default the package includes available cached USGS and USFS basemaps, contours,

00:01:22.522 --> 00:01:26.222
DEM, and AOL, plus available R2C mapping layers.

00:01:26.222 --> 00:01:29.460
Check your selections before preparing it.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:33.700
OSM and Esri basemaps and credentials are not included.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.378
On Android, connect both devices to the same Wi-Fi or hotspot, keep

00:01:38.378 --> 00:01:43.213
the package QR panel open, and have the receiver scan it in Import Config.

00:01:43.213 --> 00:01:47.199
On Apple, use Share Map Package to send the prepared ZIP; the

00:01:47.199 --> 00:01:50.009
receiver chooses the file in Import Config.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.100
Wait for the import to complete.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.890
Before departure, select the downloaded map layer and verify the area and

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:59.596
needed detail with connectivity unavailable.

00:01:59.596 --> 00:02:04.517
On each receiving device, confirm the imported map and terrain data are present.

00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:07.900
Review the results before relying on them in the field.
